Dear Dietrich, 

thanks for sending me the data off the ML. That's an other typo I did not spot: for non-genetic data (data.frame, matrix arguments), the group argument is named 'grp', and not 'pop' as for the genind method. So you need to use:
dapc <- dapc(data, grp=grp$grp, n.pca=NULL, n.da=NULL)

Cheers

Thibaut
